# ─── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every .env is ignored, including per-package ones. Only .env.example files
# are tracked, and those hold placeholders. If you ever need to commit a real
# credential to make something work, that is a design bug — fix the design.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
credentials.json
service-account*.json
secrets.json

# ─── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ─── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dist/ matters more than usual here: Vite inlines every VITE_* env var into
# the bundle at build time, so a committed dist/ leaks whatever .env was
# present when it was built.
dist/
dist-electron/
build/
out/
release/
*.asar
*.exe
*.dmg
*.AppImage
*.deb
*.snap

# ─── Runtime data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Disk-backed caches (KV + images) and anything the pipeline writes at runtime.
.data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ─── Business data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real inventory, orders, manifests, and bookkeeping exports. Sample fixtures
# live in code (noltech-pipeline/src/providers/fixtures.js), not in files here.
*.csv
!**/sample-*.csv
!**/example-*.csv
manifests/
exports/
backups/

# ─── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ─── Editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── Local agent config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
